## Experiment 4: Navigation Between Food Ordering Screens

In this experiment, navigation functionality was implemented in the Food Ordering App. A food ordering application contains multiple screens, so users need to move between pages easily. Flutter provides the Navigator class for managing navigation between different routes.

The application was divided into different screens such as Home, Restaurant/Menu, Food Details, Cart, Order Form, and Order Status. Navigator.push() can be used to open a new screen, while Navigator.pop() can be used to return to the previous screen.

Named Routes were also used to organize navigation in a structured way. Named routes make it easier to manage multiple screens in a larger application. Each important screen can be assigned a route name and opened using Navigator.pushNamed().

Data can also be passed between screens. For example, when a user selects a food item from the menu, information such as the food name, price, image, and description can be passed to the food details screen.

This experiment helped create the complete navigation flow of the Food Ordering App, allowing users to move from browsing restaurants and food items to viewing the cart and placing an order.

